olu_01SjFGtC1MQYJot1deAwiSt9", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23347, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SjFGtC1MQYJot1deAwiSt9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 27198, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all three regions. I checked afterward: all regions are on v2.3.0 and the health checks pass.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes what happened, the rollback and the stalled first attempt. It also lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n  - Look into why the orchestrator stopped the rollback partway.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01FVeKYyfFdFPo7uQam8QrBm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01W8kB4dREuNXUez8DCw47ah", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019URLjkkYMToFTishyMAcNY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MUeB2AwRCaAtGuWJNTx2Rv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0 but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll try once more, since rolling back to the same version should be safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FwbfCNRdJ1WjficYzfiBr3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YQVT6zmLhVgBHdqPx3VVYU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Ud42R1VfGuedrRWbCYAX5K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SjFGtC1MQYJot1deAwiSt9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. All 3 regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures, look into the orchestrator partial-rollout error, and find out why v2.3.1 went to production when its RC was unhealthy in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is back on v2.3.0 in all regions and healthy again. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-east on v2.3.0 and us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all three regions. I checked afterward: all regions are on v2.3.0 and the health checks pass.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. It describes what happened, the rollback and the stalled first attempt. It also lists three follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 is failing.\n  - Look into why the orchestrator stopped the rollback partway.\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 went to production when its release candidate was unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}